401:jgt22401-math-0007 for Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0008 a polynomial, Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0009, and Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0010 matrices associated to a graph Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0011. It turns out that, essentially, this can only happen if Image: urn:x-wiley:03649024:media:jgt22401:jgt22401-math-0012 is either regular or biregular.\n\nREFERENCES\n\n  * 1 A. E. Brouwer and W. H. Haemers, Spectra of Graphs, Springer Science & Business Media (2011).\n\nGoogle Scholar\n\n  * 2 S. Butler and F. Chung, Spectral graph Theory, Handbook of Linear Algebra (2006), 47.\n\nGoogle Scholar\n\n  * 3 D. Cvetković and S. K. Simić, Towards a spectral theory of graphs based on the signless laplacian, II, Linear Algebra and its Applications 432 (2010), 2257–2272.\n\nWeb of Science® Google Scholar\n\n  * 4 R. P. Stanley, Variations on differential posets, Institute for Mathematics and Its Applications 19 (1990), 145.\n\nGoogle Scholar\n\n  * 5 R. P. Stanley, Algebraic Combinatorics, Springer, New York (2013).\n\n\nVolume90, Issue3\n\nMarch 2019\n\nPages 288-303\n\n\nSpiro S. Polynomial relations between matrices of graphs. J Graph Theory. 2019; 90: 288–303. https://doi.org/10.1002/jgt.22401--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ngraphs and networks - Eigenvalue / Eigenvector Calculation - Mathematica Stack Exchange (https://mathematica.stackexchange.com/questions/11731/eigenvalue-eigenvector-calculation/11741)\nciteturn2search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 14.1 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; The square roots ought to give us pause: they are likely a significant complication in performing the arithmetic. ...     {l, z} = f[VertexDegree[g], AdjacencyMatrix[g]]; // AbsoluteTiming\n## 2 Answers\n\nSorted by:\n\n[Select]\n\nThis answer is useful\n\n[Input]\n\n11\n\nThis answer is not useful\n\n[Input]\n\nSave this answer.\n\nLoading when this answer was accepted…\n\nShow activity on this post.\n\nFor speeding up Mathematica code, a little analysis of a problem often goes a long way.\n\n### Analysis\n\nWriting $\\mathbb{G}$ for the diagonal matrix of vertex degrees and $\\mathbb{A}$ for the adjacency matrix, this question seeks eigenvectors of $\\mathbb{1} - \\mathbb{G}^{-1/2} \\mathbb{A} \\mathbb{G}^{-1/2}$. That is, it looks for solutions $(\\mathbf{z}, \\lambda)$ to\n\n$$\\mathbf{z} \\left(\\mathbb{1} - \\mathbb{G}^{-1/2} \\mathbb{A} \\mathbb{G}^{-1/2} \\right) = \\lambda \\mathbf{z}.$$\n\nThe square roots ought to give us pause: they are likely a significant complication in performing the arithmetic.\n\nIt is straightforward to rewrite this system of equations, though, as\n\n$$\\left(\\mathbf{z} \\mathbb{G}^{1/2}\\right)\\left(\\mathbb{G^{-1} A}\\right) = \\left(1-\\lambda\\right)\\left(\\mathbf{z}\\mathbb{G}^{1/2}\\right).$$\n\nWhence, if we solve\n\n$$\\mathbf{w}\\left(\\mathbb{G^{-1} A}\\right) = \\mu \\mathbf{w}$$\n\nthen $\\lambda = 1-\\mu$ and $\\mathbf{z} = \\mathbf{w} \\mathbb{G}^{-1/2}$. The square roots come in only at the end as easy matrix multiplications, while $\\mathbb{GA}$ is a rational matrix. Hopefully, calculations involving it will be faster.\n\n### Solution\n\nHere is an implementation:\n    \n    `f[g_, a_] := Module[{e, v},\n       {e, v} = Eigensystem[DiagonalMatrix[1/g] . a];\n       {1 - e, v.DiagonalMatrix[Sqrt[g]]}\n       ];\n    `\n\nLet's carry it out on the example data:\n    \n    `g = ExampleData[{\"NetworkGraph\", \"ZacharysKarateClub\"}];\n    {l, z} = f[VertexDegree[g], AdjacencyMatrix[g]]; // AbsoluteTiming\n    `\n\n> {31.8538219, Null}\n\n* * *\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOn the Extended Adjacency Eigenvalues of Graphs and Applications (https://www.mdpi.com/2227-7390/13/22/3620)\nciteturn2search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Since the grap